	N-gram Language Models
	
Language Model assigns a probability to each possible next word, or equivalently
gives a probability distribution over possible next words.

N-gram language model : -> It is a sequence of n words: 2-gram ia two-word
sequence of words like "The Water" or "water of". This is a probabilist model
that can estimate the probability of a word given the n-1 previous words.

P(w|s)= C(s + w)/C(s)
w = word and s = sequence of words

